# Data immutability (raw is read-only)

Treat `data/raw/` as **immutable** source-of-truth. Never edit, overwrite, “fix in place”, or delete original raw files.

## Rules
- Never modify any file under `data/raw/` (including by writing back a cleaned CSV with the same name).
- If a raw file has issues, document them and apply cleaning **in code** or write a new artifact elsewhere.
- All derived artifacts must be written to one of:
  - `data/interim/` (lightly cleaned, standardized schema, still close to raw)
  - `data/processed/` (model-ready tables/features)
  - `reports/figures/` (plots)
  - `cache/` (API downloads / cached responses)
- When you must persist a cleaned dataset, write a **new** file with a new name/version and keep the raw untouched.

## Notebook expectation
- Loading cells should read from `data/raw/`.
- Cleaning/feature engineering should return new DataFrames (no in-place edits of raw frames).
- Save outputs to `data/interim/` or `data/processed/` with explicit timestamps/versions when helpful.

